tags: bitcoin-p2wpkh

A payment contract on Bitcoin: p2wpkh, pay-to-witness-public-key-hash.

ContractRate.mu_per_unit gives the MU for one satoshi. The script attribute is the
scriptPubKey that receives the payment. The token_id attribute is "BTC". The script
and token_id attributes are required. The address attribute is only for a person: the
script attribute decides.

To pay, make one transaction. It must have one output to the script attribute with
the amount or more, in satoshi. It must also have one OP_RETURN output. Its data is the
deposit token in UTF-8, 80 bytes or less. The payee accepts the payment when the
transaction has the number of confirmations that the payee selects (a payee parameter,
payment.min_confirmations, not a part of this formal).

=== formal
payment.accepted=the transaction is confirmed; the payee selects how many confirmations
payment.deposit_token=an OP_RETURN output of the same transaction; its data is the UTF-8 deposit token, at most 80 bytes
payment.kind=p2wpkh: pay-to-witness-public-key-hash
payment.output=one output to payment.xattr.script with at least the amount, in satoshi
payment.rate.unit=ContractRate.mu_per_unit is MU per satoshi
payment.xattr.address=informative; payment.xattr.script decides
payment.xattr.required=script, token_id
payment.xattr.script=scriptPubKey bytes that receive the payment
payment.xattr.token_id=BTC
